    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "**PROPERTY COMPLETELY FREE OF PYRITE**GREEN CERT AVAILABLE ON REQUEST** \r\n\r\nHoran Estates are delighted to present this beautifully maintained four bedroom, 3 bathroom semi detached residence to the Dublin property market.  Ideally located in the highly sought-after development of New Haven Bay, Balbriggan, this property boats a host of features.\r\n\r\nPresented in excellent walk-in condition throughout, this bright and spacious home has been pyrite remediated recently and is like a brand new house as a result. The property spans three floors and is perfect for all types of purchasers, from those who're first time mortgage approved, to investors or those looking to trade up or down. Space is certainly not an issue in this property with a large sitting room and kitchen/dining room open plan on the ground floor, three good sized bedrooms (one ensuite) on the first floor and an additional bedroom with an ensuite and velux windows on the top floor.\r\n\r\nBalbriggan is home to the Irish Institute of Music and Song and their popular and attractive Lark Theatre. \r\nThe M1 motorway is five minutes’ drive from the subject property providing very easy access to the Dublin International Airport, Port Tunnel and the city centre. Balbriggan train station is within walking distance from the development offering daily services to and from the city centre and its suburbs. \r\n\r\nContact as soon as possible as this property is unlikely to be available for long."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "- Suits both first time purchasers and investors\r\n- Highly sought after area\r\n- Excellent transport links within easy reach of the property\r\n- Private Garden to the rear, ample space for parking to the front\r\n- Gas fired central heating\r\n- Three Generous Double Bedrooms – 10 sq. m, 12.64 sq. m, 13sqm in size \r\n- Generously proportioned living areas and bedrooms\r\n- Abundance of natural light throughout the building\r\n- Easy access to the M50, M1 and Dublin airport\r\n- Mix of laminate wooden floors and carpets throughout, windows are all double glazed"
      },
      {
